menu "SCB PCB V2 wiring"
config SCB_MOTOR_PCB_ROUTING
    bool "Use motor STEP/DIR pad nets from the supplied PCB layout"
    default y
    help
        The supplied schematic says X STEP=34 DIR=35, Y STEP=36 DIR=37.
        Its PCB swaps STEP and DIR on both axes. The user confirmed fabrication
        from that PCB: keep enabled. Disable only for schematic-wired hardware.
config SCB_SENSOR_NAMED_WIRING
    bool "Sensor cable is crossed by signal NAME rather than pin number"
    default n
    help
        Default is a normal IDC16 pin-number-preserving cable (J4.n -> J1.n).
        Master and sensor boards have different signal labels at the same pins.
        Enable ONLY when the cable is verified to cross each signal by name.
endmenu
